Minimum Requirements:
Earned Diploma [KNQF level 6] certificate in Automotive Engineering;Technician or its equivalent;
Two (2) Years’ experience in similar position;Licensed by TVETA
Registered by Engineer Board of Kenya (E.B.K) or Kenya Engineering Technology
Registration Board (KETRB);
Strong analytical and communication skills;
Patient, supportive, and passionate about learning;In depth knowledge of the tertiary training structure and CBET;
Exposure to TVET CDACC;
Key Responsibilities
Instruct trainees in the specific course(s)/units in adherence to the respective curriculum and occupational standards;
Plan, conduct and assess practicals in the course units assigned;
Prepare internal assessments, mark, grade, conduct validation and moderation;
Supervise and assess trainee(s) in the course area and during industrial attachment;
Maintaining appropriate records required by TVETA and TVET CDACC or any other relevant body including learning, session plans, training notes and records of work;
Any other duty as may be assigned by the Coordinator or Director;
