Job Specifications
Officers will be responsible to their Head of Directorate, for design and development and maintenance of public transport infrastructure within the Nairobi Metropolitan Area (NMA).
Duties and Responsibilities
Coordinating the development and implementation of MRTS and NMT policies, strategies, standards, procedures and guidelines;
Overseeing the development and maintenance of MRTS and NMT infrastructure and associated facilities;
Ensuring MRTS and NMT services are integrated with other modes of public transport;
Liaising with the implementing entities to ensure development works are delivered as per schedule and to the specified quality;
Overseeing priority programmes and project implementation through set timelines, budgets and resource allocation;
Ensuring the preparation of periodic programmes and projects reports;
Spearheading the Identification of MRTS and NMT Infrastructure development priority areas for funding;
Coordinating the preparation of funding proposals for projects and programmes;
Overseeing the preparation of contracts for MRTS and NMT infrastructure development;
Partnering with external finance agencies for resource mobilization and developing various project financing models;
Coordinating the preparation of tender specifications and documents for MRTS and NMT infrastructure works;
Reviewing the generated reports on projects and programmes;
Coordinating the identification and preparation of list of lead actors for corporate resource mobilization;
Reviewing policies, analytic briefs and reports;
Overseeing the integration of Public Transport and land use planning in the Nairobi Metropolitan Area (NMA); and
Overseeing the design development and maintenance of MRTS stations, depots and associated Infrastructure.
Person Specifications
For appointment to this grade a candidate must have: -
A minimum period of ten (10) years in relevant work experience and at least three (3) years in supervisory role in a position in the Public Service or Private Sector;
Master’s degree in Civil Engineering, Architecture, Project Management/Construction
Management or any other relevant qualifications;
Bachelor’s degree in Civil Engineering, Architecture, Project Management/Construction Management or Equivalent qualifications;
Management course lasting not less than four (4) weeks from a recognized institution;
Membership/Registration of a professional body in good standing where applicable; and
Proficiency in computer applications
