Requirements for Appointment:
To be eligible for appointment to the position of Lecturer, the candidate must have:
A Bachelor’s degree in Clinical Medicine from an accredited/recognized institution;
A Master’s degree in Clinical Medicine from an accredited/recognized institution;
At least 3 years of relevant working experience;
Evidence of recognition and registration by the relevant regulatory body where applicable; and
Evidence of membership or affiliation of the relevant professional body where applicable.
PhD will be an added advantage.
DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
An individual appointed as a Lecturer shall:
Teach and asses courses in one’s discipline at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels;
Supervise undergraduate students’ projects and other experimental learning programmes;
Supervise dissertations/theses at postgraduate level;
Participate in the development/review of undergraduate and postgraduate courses;
Initiate, promote and participate in research projects;
Provide professional and community services, and initiate strategic training and research partnerships and linkages, and undertake fundraising for the university; and
Carry out administrative and such other duties and responsibilities as may be assigned from time to time.
go to method of application »

Requirements for Appointment:
To be eligible for appointment and/or promotion to the position of Senior Lecturer the candidate must have:
A Doctorate degree (PhD) or its academic equivalent from an accredited/recognized institution;
